  "notes": "University Park. Verified 2026-08-27 against the department's real Advising Handbook (rev 2026.08.13, https://www.che.psu.edu/assets/docs/handbooks/undergrad-handbook.pdf), not just the bulletin. 'Chemical engineering elective' and 'Lab experience' are wired to the handbook's own explicit, enumerated course lists (page 14). 'Professional elective' (handbook: 'broad category... enhance your portfolio of professional skills... typically 200-level or above') is wired via open_elective at 200+, excluding MATH/PHYS/CHEM as an inference (not explicitly denylisted in the handbook, but implausible as a 'professional development' pick) -- ENGR added to departments since the handbook explicitly names ENGR co-op/leadership courses for this category. 'Engineering elective', 'Science elective', and 'Science or engineering elective' are LEFT AS GENERIC UNWIRED PLACEHOLDERS ON PURPOSE: the handbook does give explicit finite department+number lists for these (its own page-14 'LIST OF ENGINEERING, SCIENCE and LAB ELECTIVES'), spanning ~15-20 departments each, several of which (ACS, ABE, ASTRO, BIOE, ENVSE, ESC, FSC, IST, MNG, NUCE, PNG, SCM) have no catalog file in this repo -- rather than fabricate an approximate course list from memory, left unwired pending either a fuller catalog scrape or the exact page-14 list being re-extracted. Fixed 3 real discrepancies against the current bulletin/handbook: ECON 102/104 and a generic Gen Ed were swapped between Semester 1/2 (bulletin has ECON in Fall, Gen Ed in Spring) -- corrected. CHEM 110/EDSGN 100/MATH 141 were missing the bulletin's own '#' Entrance-to-Major flag (already present on MATH 140/PHYS 211) -- added. ENGL 202C is the only Additional Course the CHE-specific bulletin plan names (no 202A/B/D equivalence documented) -- narrowed. Post-prereq-parser-fix repair (unrelated to the handbook review, left largely as-is): CHEM 110's real catalog prereq is MATH 22, which chains through MATH 21 -- MATH 21/MATH 22 (Semester 2) act as an engine-only fallback for a hypothetical student with no reported math placement (see expand_math_placement in planner_engine.py); for a realistic incoming student who places into MATH 140 (as every CHE student does), this waives instantly and the plan schedules cleanly in the real 8-semester length. Removed 2026-08-27: MATH 3 and MATH 4 (previously in Semester 1) -- math_catalog.json's own MATH 21 entry has an empty prereq_groups (no prerequisite at all), and MATH 3/MATH 4 are separately hardcoded as unconditionally satisfied everywhere by expand_math_placement regardless of any student input. Removing them (verified via build_full_plan) also resolves the previously-flagged 'needs 10 simulated terms, not 8' issue for a realistic placement-tier student -- confirmed clean at 8 terms of real coursework (one greedy-scheduler credit-packing artifact spills 9 leftover elective credits into a light 9th term, a pre-existing scheduler behavior unrelated to the math chain, not further patched here).",
